      "read": false,
      "user_title": null,
      "bookmarked": false,
      "raw": "Yeah, the damage is still coming from the same thing - Nightmist (or anyone else, for that matter) redirecting the damage isn&#39;t &quot;picking up&quot; that damage and then throwing it at someone else - she&#39;s putting up a big arrow pointing in a different direction so the damage goes over there instead - it doesn&#39;t make it [i]her[/i] damage. Nemesis bonus is also recalculated if the target changes - Gloomy tries to hit Nightmist so the damage is increased as he&#39;s her Nemesis, but she uses the Amulet to redirect. The damage is no longer hitting Nightmist, so the Nemesis bonus goes away.\n",
